  - id: knowledge_of_god
    displayName: Knowledge of God
    flavorText: The LORD declares He desires mercy and the knowledge of God rather
      than burnt offerings, words Jesus later quotes twice against the Pharisees.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Declares that steadfast covenant love and relational knowledge of God
      matter more to the LORD than ritual sacrifice, one of the book's central theological
      statements and among the most quoted verses in the Minor Prophets.
    deliveredByManagerId: hosea
    managerId: mercy_not_sacrifice
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
